\n  \\\"task_id\\\": \\\"RS-DRIVER-PERFECT-HCM0-RESULT-REVIEW-ROUTING\\\",\\n  \\\"title\\\": \\\"Driver Perfect HCM0 successor result review and routing\\\",\\n  \\\"kind\\\": \\\"GOVERNANCE\\\",\\n  \\\"owner\\\": \\\"driver/governance/perfect-hcm0-review-routing\\\",\\n  \\\"base_state\\\": \\\"READY\\\",\\n  \\\"priority\\\": \\\"P0\\\",\\n  \\\"leverage\\\": \\\"HIGH\\\",\\n  \\\"frontier\\\": \\\"The superseded HCM0 exploration has split into two immutable claimable research successors—extreme-branch parity domination and tangent-face induction—sharing one frozen handoff index. Driver continuity now requires exact-set result intake, scoped review, reconciliation if multiple reviews/results appear, and follow-up or parent-routing without reopening closed routes.\\\",\\n  \\\"next_action\\\": \\\"Read the frozen HCM0 handoff index and the two pinned successor publications; on every control entry refresh their current result/review state, consume any frozen Result at exact scope, and materialize the required review/follow-up or exact-set synthesis without duplicating already-published research.\\\",\\n  \\\"dependencies\\\": [\\n    \\\"TP2-4F8D04C54528CFF5E1B2\\\",\\n    \\\"TP2-52A743E08EFB309FE47C\\\",\\n    \\\"OG-9CD71978EC19A9D5B7FA\\\"\\n  ],\\n  \\\"source_refs\\\": [\\n    \\\"git:awdawmip/enterprise-math@623a4ee81911cc79d07ed5db1887a06ebe91ffd5:research_artifacts/PERFECT_PRIME_AP_SIGNED_SECANT_HCM0_HAUSDORFF_LIFT/HCM0_RESEARCH_HANDOFF_INDEX_20260909.md\\\",\\n    \\\"git:awdawmip/enterprise-math@fa34f1334d522201701210db932f75a916bdc148:research_task_records/RS-PERFECT-PRIME-AP-HCM0-EXTREME-BRANCH-PARITY-DOMINATION/TP2-4F8D04C54528CFF5E1B2.json\\\",\\n    \\\"git:awdawmip/enterprise-math@fa34f1334d522201701210db932f75a916bdc148:research_task_records/RS-PERFECT-PRIME-AP-HCM0-TANGENT-FACE-INDUCTION/TP2-52A743E08EFB309FE47C.json\\\",\\n    \\\"git:awdawmip/enterprise-math@fa34f1334d522201701210db932f75a916bdc148:research_objective_heads/OBJ-ROUTE-A-PERFECT-PRIME-TABLE-CRITICAL-COFACTOR-ALL-M.json\\\"\\n  ],\\n  \\\"evidence_status\\\": \\\"HCM0_PARENT_OPEN / TWO_RESEARCH_SUCCESSORS_ACTIVE / DURABLE_HANDOFF_INDEX_FROZEN\\\",\\n  \\\"last_progress_ref\\\": \\\"git:awdawmip/enterprise-math@623a4ee81911cc79d07ed5db1887a06ebe91ffd5:research_artifacts/PERFECT_PRIME_AP_SIGNED_SECANT_HCM0_HAUSDORFF_LIFT/HCM0_RESEARCH_HANDOFF_INDEX_20260909.md\\\",\\n  \\\"last_progress_at\\\": \\\"2026-09-09T01:14:18+00:00\\\",\\n  \\\"hard_block\\\": \\\"AWAIT_CHILD_RESULT_OR_RECONCILE_NEW_CONTROL_EVIDENCE\\\",\\n  \\\"tags\\\": [\\n    \\\"Driver\\\",\\n    \\\"Perfect-Prime\\\",\\n    \\\"HCM0\\\",\\n    \\\"review\\\",\\n    \\\"handoff\\\",\\n    \\\"exact-set\\\"\\n  ],\\n  \\\"claim_lease_minutes\\\": 360,\\n  \\\"created_by_role\\\": \\\"RESEARCH_DRIVER\\\",\\n  \\\"task_authority\\\": \\\"PUBLISHED_REGISTERED\\\",\\n  \\\"publication_contract\\\": \\\"RESEARCH_TASK_PUBLICATION_V1\\\",\\n  \\\"publication_template\\\": \\\"RESEARCH_TASK_PUBLICATION_TEMPLATE_V1\\\",\\n  \\\"registry_key\\\": \\\"RS-DRIVER-PERFECT-HCM0-RESULT-REVIEW-ROUTING\\\",\\n  \\\"parent_objective_id\\\": \\\"OBJ-DRIVER-PERFECT-NCOUPLED-CONTINUITY-20260909\\\",\\n  \\\"parent_objective_generation_id\\\": \\\"OG-7C8A91D4E2B5063F18C7\\\",\\n  \\\"identity_policy\\\": \\\"AUTO_RESOLVE_OR_ALLOCATE\\\",\\n  \\\"final_response_identity_policy\\\": \\\"INHERIT_GLOBAL\\\",\\n  \\\"identity_lane\\\": \\\"DRV-HCM0\\\",\\n  \\\"origin_kind\\\": \\\"DIRECT_USER_DIRECTION\\\",\\n  \\\"task_lineage\\\": \\\"NEW_DIRECTION\\\",\\n  \\\"parent_task_id\\\": null,\\n  \\\"successor_gate\\\": null,\\n  \\\"policy_review\\\": {\\n    \\\"policy_set\\\": \\\"research_taskbook_policy.json\\\",\\n    \\\"policy_digest\\\": \\\"sha256:dd425305887871866cb2f0894885ff38359639e2de7750fa45e8c584e19feae4\\\",\\n    \\\"review_state\\\": \\\"PASS\\\",\\n    \\\"temporary_overrides\\\": []\\n  }\\n}\\n-->\\n\\n# Driver Perfect HCM0 successor result review and routing\\n\\nStatus: `READY / DRIVER-PUBLISHED GOVERNANCE`\\n\\n## 0. Mother question\\n\\nHow should a successor Driver preserve exact control continuity for the open Perfect Prime HCM0 route after the former broad HCM0 task was superseded by two complementary research successors, while preventing duplicate review, stale-route replay, or accidental strengthening of the parent theorem?\\n\\n## 1. Frozen inputs and scope\\n\\nThe mathematical parent objective remains open. The current research entrypoints are exactly:\\n\\n- `RS-PERFECT-PRIME-AP-HCM0-EXTREME-BRANCH-PARITY-DOMINATION / TP2-4F8D04C54528CFF5E1B2`;\\n- `RS-PERFECT-PRIME-AP-HCM0-TANGENT-FACE-INDUCTION / TP2-52A743E08EFB309FE47C`.\\n\\nBefore any Driver decision, consume `git:awdawmip/enterprise-math@623a4ee81911cc79d07ed5db1887a06ebe91ffd5:research_artifacts/PERFECT_PRIME_AP_SIGNED_SECANT_HCM0_HAUSDORFF_LIFT/HCM0_RESEARCH_HANDOFF_INDEX_20260909.md`. Its all-`m` theorem list is frozen reusable input, its finite evidence must remain finite-only, and its closed-route list must not be reopened without genuinely new information.\\n\\nThis is a control task, not a mathematical proof task. It grants no theorem strength. Do not create a second research successor merely because one child finishes. Do not choose one Result as authoritative by recency when multiple immutable reviews/results exist.\\n\\n## 2. Hard target and required outputs\\n\\nHard target: `PERFECT_HCM0_SUCCESSOR_RESULTS_EXACTLY_REVIEWED_RECONCILED_AND_ROUTED`.\\n\\nOn each control entry:\\n\\n1. Refresh the two pinned research publications and their live Result/review state.\\n2. If neither has a frozen Result, preserve both research entrypoints and return the exact waiting frontier without inventing a review.\\n3. If one or both have frozen Results, verify the complete Result envelope and scope before mathematical review.\\n4. If exactly one operational review authority exists for a Result, use it; if multiple immutable reviews exist, resolve the exact review set through the required reference/synthesis path before operational follow-up.\\n5. Decide whether the accepted child theorem/obstruction advances only one extreme coefficient/face, proves all HCM0 cells, produces an exact counterexample, or merely kills a local route.\\n6. Materialize the required follow-up taskset or separately justified mathematical parent-objective action. Never infer parent closure from a child PASS alone.\\n7. Update the durable Driver handoff with exact current publication/review identifiers and the smallest unfinished unit.\\n\\n## 3. Research value to preserve\\n\\nThe HCM0 exploration has accumulated many valid all-`m` reductions and exact no-go boundaries. The main control risk is now loss of provenance during handoff: a new Driver could repeat closed routes, promote bounded computations, or treat one complementary child as if it settled the whole determinant problem. This task keeps the two child routes and their review authority synchronized without merging their mathematical claims prematurely.\\n\\n## 4. Success, kill, and return criteria\\n\\nSuccess is a durable Driver disposition for every frozen child Result encountered, with exact-set reconciliation where required, correct follow-up materialization, and a handoff that points to the current smallest unfinished mathematical unit.\\n\\nIf no child Result exists, return `WAITING_ON_PINNED_CHILD_RESEARCH` with the two publication identifiers and do not fabricate work. Kill any attempt to reopen the superseded broad HCM0 task as the current research entrypoint, to promote finite `m` evidence to all-`m`, to collapse signed parity provenance, or to close the Perfect parent objective without a theorem/counterexample at its exact scope.\\n\\nThis governance task is terminal only when no unresolved Driver action remains for the two pinned child routes and control has been explicitly handed to a later routed research/control unit.\\n\"},\"server_comments\":1195,\"source_sha\":\"456c6f38e9c3a310d9a809fcea1b112832